          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Bumble kills the swipe and bets on AI matchmaking assistant 'Bee' to reinvent online dating",
            "articleSection": "Daily Utility",
            "abstract": "Bumble CEO Whitney Wolfe Herd announced the dating app is eliminating its signature swipe mechanic and pivoting toward AI-driven matchmaking, including a new AI dating assistant called Bee. The company is positioning AI as a 'supercharger to love and relationships', signalling a fundamental redesign of how hundreds of millions of users interact with the platform. The move marks one of the most high-profile consumer AI pivots in the social app space, with implications for how AI agents may mediate personal relationships at scale.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/07/bumble-is-getting-rid-of-the-swipe-ceo-says/",
            "publisher": {
              "@type": "NewsMediaOrganization",
              "name": "The AI Chronicle",
